    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20326" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hĕdĕrātus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕd-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adorned</i> or <i>crowned with ivy</i>: patina
			argentea, Gall. ap. Treb. <i><span class="en">Claud. 17</span></i>
			dub. (Peter, hederaceam): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nemes. Ecl. 3, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pompae,</span>”
				<i>Bacchic</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 26, 278</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Liber,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Cor. Mil. 7</span></i>
			.</div>
